[BLEND a_m=0.83 a_c=0.83 wrote=1] Compute ln(0).
A: The natural logarithm of zero is undefined.

In mathematics, the natural logarithm (logarithm in base e) is a mathematical function describing the inverse of the exponential function with base e. The natural logarithm of a number is the power to which e must be raised to produce that number.

The natural logarithm of zero is undefined because there is no positive real number to which e can be raised to produce zero.

In other words, the natural logarithm of zero is not a real number.

